{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted","id":1129502,"title":"Increasing the number of Lunar Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T17:44:51-07:00","id":1129502,"title":"Increasing the number of Lunar Exalted","content":"So, I am wondering what type of effect (if any) does everyone think would occur if we increased the number of Lunar Essences to 900? Since there are three times as many Solar Essences as Sidereal Essence, it seems to me that there would be a nice symmetry if there were three times as many Lunar Essences as there were Solar Essences. Of course, it would mean that the Lunar Exalted of the First Age would have been roughly divided into three groups (Consorts and Lovers for the Solar Kings and Queens of the Old Realm, Admirals and Generals for the military of the Old Realm, and Scouts and Spies who would act as an early warning system for threats to the Old Realm), but I do not think that it would really matter that much other than giving more diversity to the opinions of modern Lunar Exalted about the ancient Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Do you think such an increase would make the Lunar Exalted too much of a threat for the Realm? What other effects do you think increasing the number of Lunar Essences would have? Do you think that such an increase would be a good idea or do you think that the current number is adequate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:40:24-07:00","id":1129544,"title":"","content":"I can't speak from experience with 3rd on this, as the Lunar's book is not out yet. So bear in mind my opinion is based on the 2e Manual of Exalted Power.<br /> <br /> I say its your game, do it if it works for you. However, one thing to keep in mind is that the Lunars get a lot of bang for their buck charm wise. The Lunar Ox-Body Technique gave six health levels in 2e. One Ox-Body charm and you've nearly doubled your health levels. Most other Exalts had to take two or three Ox-Body's to get their health doubled like that. Lunar Excellencies are also Attribute based, so they go a pretty long distance in terms of what you can do with them. If your comfortable with having an additional 600 of these exalts in your game, go for it and see how it turns out. Overall I don't think changing the numbers will have much effect on the game, its just 600 more possible exalts and you can't play them all the same time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6162-raven79","name":"Raven79","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6162_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:55:02-07:00","id":1129692,"title":"","content":"You have now compounded the problem of why the Lunars have accomplished essentially nothing in 2000 years. While the Caul is a new thing they did, for the most part the world has been the Terrestrials' playground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:14:20-07:00","id":1129717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129692#post1129692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have now compounded the problem of why the Lunars have accomplished essentially nothing in 2000 years. While the Caul is a new thing they did, for the most part the world has been the Terrestrials' playground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Holden stressed that isn't the case in 3E, and in fact Lunars sabotage is a huge part of the reason Dragon-Blooded infrastructure hasn't gotten past late antiquity level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:55:34-07:00","id":1129721,"title":"","content":"I'd wonder, being outnumbered 3 to 1 by Lunars, how the Solars managed to be in charge of the Old Realm, and didn't have to share power with the Lunars as equals. Solars are more powerful than Lunars; but they're not<i> that</i> much more powerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, in the modern day, I'd say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think such an increase would make the Lunar Exalted too much of a threat for the Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes............<br /> but honestly, it's not like we can really measure these things. There's no particular way to say &quot;X DBs are equal to Y Lunars&quot;. We just assume 15000 Realm DBs and 400 Lunars are roughly matched. If the books said &quot;15000 Realm DBs and 900 Lunars are roughly matched&quot;... okay? You can't measure that, really.<br /> <br /> I mean, if suddenly Luna exalted 500 new Lunars, then the plot would be that the Realm is in deep trouble, yeah.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that such an increase would be a good idea or do you think that the current number is adequate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the current number is adequate. Firstly, it's enough that the Solar Bond is a thing, but if you really hate it (as some Lunar players do) you can play someone who doesn't have one.<br /> Secondly, it gives you about 100-150 of each caste, which I think is a good number.<br /> Or, to put it away, there's about 100 per direction (or maybe 80, plus 80 for the River Province) which I think is plenty.<br /> <br /> Currently, for the area level I tend to use for games (generally about 2 million square miles), I reckon about 5 Lunars (ie one pack) is reasonable, plus PCs, perhaps a bit more if I want, with 100 per direction. So most recently, I had one Lunar pack of 4 or 5, 1 Lunar behind the throne of Harborhead, 1 Lunar on the throne of his own city-state, and 2 Lunar PCs.<br /> That's a little high, but it's fine, because it's a dramatic area where dramatic stuff is happening, and presumably there's plenty of 2 million square mile areas of boring desert with like 1 or 2 Lunars.<br /> <br /> My friend's game is a bit smaller (just 3-4 smaller countries next to each other, south-west of Prasad), so there's just our Lunar PCs, but there's another Lunar pack to our east (where my Lunar's gone to be tattooed), so the number's roughly the same. Essentially, one Lunar pack for the west of the Dreaming Sea region.<br /> <br /> Anyway, 8 or 9 Lunars in an exciting, active area of about 2m square miles seems a bit high when there's 100 Lunars per direction, but it's okay because of all the blank areas, so the number is about right, I think.<br /> <br /> If there was 900 Lunars, then we'd be talking over 200 Lunars per direction. That'd be a lot more areas per game area (like, the Dreaming Sea would probably have about 50 Lunars, which I think is way too many), and I'd feel like I'd have to put in a lot more Lunar characters... but I don't really want to.<br /> (One of the key lessons I learnt when running 2nd ed is not to have too many Exalts: instead, use a small number of Exalts but put more effort into making them cool, interesting, and evocative, with effects on the societies around them. Having the Abyssal, Solar or Lunar of the week makes Exalts generic and uninspiring. Each one should be a world-shaker, not a throw-away NPC. Thus, I don't want to have too many Celestials per game. In my 2nd ed game, I think the PCs met something like 50+ Celestials, in my 3rd ed game, they met about 12, but I bet they can remember more about the 3rd ed Celestials than the 2nd ed ones, because they were more interesting and had effects on the world around them)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if that's very clear, but I hope you guys can see what I'm getting at.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:32:48-07:00","id":1129728,"title":"","content":"There are no set numbers this edition. So the old figures off 300-300-100 dont necessarily apply anymore. In fact, it may be now there is no ratio between them at all, especially with Solar Bond not being a thing anymore<br /> <br /> I wouldnt go with 900 though (a few too many), but more Lunars than Solars totally works in my books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:03:00-07:00","id":1129735,"title":"","content":"I think there still are set numbers; they're just a bit vague.<br /> <br /> There are about 150 Solars. There are about 400 Lunars (might be 390, might be 415, but it's about 400). There's probably about 100 Abyssals, approx.<br /> <br /> There's about 25000 DBs, IIRC?<br /> <br /> Though I think there probably will be exactly 100 Sidereals (but of course, in reality there's about 90ish, because some are unexalted).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:09:51-07:00","id":1129737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129728#post1129728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> especially with Solar Bond not being a thing anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>The bond is still a thing. It is just that it is now an option rather than the default setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T04:42:53-07:00","id":1129746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129692#post1129692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have now compounded the problem of why the Lunars have accomplished essentially nothing in 2000 years. While the Caul is a new thing they did, for the most part the world has been the Terrestrials' playground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this.<br /> Honestly to me, the Lunar problem has always been one of tone. They (and thus a lot of their fanbase) don't seem to consider their enemies as being worthy of them, this means when they fail (which they must, at least until RY 768) there's no saving face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T05:20:32-07:00","id":1129752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129721#post1129721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wonder, being outnumbered 3 to 1 by Lunars, how the Solars managed to be in charge of the Old Realm, and didn't have to share power with the Lunars as equals. Solars are more powerful than Lunars; but they're not<i> that</i> much more powerful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What was the basis of Solar pre-eminence in the First Age specifically?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it's a matter of why Solars are in charge and Lunars aren't, I would propose that this was because being in charge was the kind of thing that many Lunars did not want and weren't very good at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129737#post1129737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just that it is now an option rather than the default setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat do you mean by that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T06:12:19-07:00","id":1129760,"title":"","content":"In a game sense raising the number of Lunars in the setting makes no practical difference. STs will use whatever number of Exalts they find entertaining or needed for their games. Besides this edition sets no hard limits on the number of Celestial Exalts that I can see beyond 'some hundreds'.<br /> <br /> Its logical effect on the setting of dramatically raising the number of Lunar Exalts is still something to consider though for many reasons explained above. I like the ratios set forth in earlier editions so don't see much reason to change it. I do see your suggested political divisions of what the Lunars would be in the 1st Age a bit rigid and unrealistic. The majority of Lunars would more than likely play multiple roles that overlapped quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T05:14:01-07:00","id":1130781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1129752#post1129752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Ex3 the bond isn't presented as a link <i>every </i>lunar <i>exaltation</i> had with a solar <i>exaltation</i>, 1:1, but as a bond that <i>might </i>be formed between two <i>exalted </i>over several excarnations. It's being set up as an opt-in rather than an opt-out story hook.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:27:26-07:00","id":1130883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1130781#post1130781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Ex3 the bond isn't presented as a link <i>every </i>lunar <i>exaltation</i> had with a solar <i>exaltation</i>, 1:1, but as a bond that <i>might </i>be formed between two <i>exalted </i>over several excarnations. It's being set up as an opt-in rather than an opt-out story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>And applicable to all Exalts? <br /> <br /> Damn, what a way to water down a thematic idea... I'd be disappointed with that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:53:11-07:00","id":1130890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1130883#post1130883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And applicable to all Exalts? <br /> <br /> Damn, what a way to water down a thematic idea... I'd be disappointed with that...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's still specifically a Lunar-Solar thing. The Lunar spread in the Ex3 core talks about how their relationship with Solars was central to their identity in the First Age, and that the reconfiguration of their Castes after the Usurpation and the deep - seated rage common to them now were both reactions to losing it -- the former a deliberate choice to be a new people in a new Age, but the latter simply a result of the new void where once there was partnership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:24:40-07:00","id":1130905,"title":"","content":"The problem with Solar Essences is that they come with memories from the previous incarnation. It is a common trait in Celestial Essences, but it is particularly important for the Solar Exalted because they may remember the fell pleasures from torturing and violating their Lunar spouses (the theme of extreme physical and psychological abuse is a common one when discussing the relationships, look at the relationship of Lilith and Desus in the First Age). While there are the few Solar Exalted who are blessed without the memories of their previous incarnations, who were the few Solar Exalted who experienced hundreds of incarnations because their Essences were not trapped within the Jade Prison, or who were the few Solar Exalted who actually loved their Lunar consorts, the majority of Solar Exalted should be haunted by the horrible things that they did to their Lunar consorts in their previous incarnation (as well as the horrible things that they did to everyone else as they devolved into corrupted God-Kings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T11:58:52-07:00","id":1130919,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... maybe, but I don't think they tend to have that many memories of the First Age. Just a few. Though I've generally left it up to the player: some of my players love first-age memories, others couldn't care less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:09:39-07:00","id":1130938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1130905#post1130905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Solar Essences is that they come with memories from the previous incarnation. It is a common trait in Celestial Essences, but it is particularly important for the Solar Exalted because they may remember the fell pleasures from torturing and violating their Lunar spouses (the theme of extreme physical and psychological abuse is a common one when discussing the relationships, look at the relationship of Lilith and Desus in the First Age). While there are the few Solar Exalted who are blessed without the memories of their previous incarnations, who were the few Solar Exalted who experienced hundreds of incarnations because their Essences were not trapped within the Jade Prison, or who were the few Solar Exalted who actually loved their Lunar consorts, the majority of Solar Exalted should be haunted by the horrible things that they did to their Lunar consorts in their previous incarnation (as well as the horrible things that they did to everyone else as they devolved into corrupted God-Kings).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an extremely fringe view of the whole thing, and not even hinted at on the book.<br /> <br /> Besides the whole \u201cpast lives memory\u201d thing being way toned down and very optional, nowhere is it suggested that most, or even many, of the relationship beween bonded Solar-Lunar mates suffered from abuse.<br /> <br /> Corrupted God-King is not another way to say sexual deviant smut snuff pr0n mustache twirler.<br /> <br /> The sheer diversity of Limit Triggers and Breaks should be enough to illustrate that the damage that might have been spread was of varied nature and intensity. From a crazed warrior king murdering a whole city because they stepped on the manicured royal lawn on their way to the harvest festival to a lord protector who stares at the mirror while his people are decimated by a fae raid because his wife failed to tell him in the morning that he was the light of her life.<br /> <br /> So no, most Solars should not be haunted and scarred by the abuse they inflicted on their Lunar Bondmates. They could be, but that is one story in thousands. Not even close to being common.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:31:44-07:00","id":1130941,"title":"","content":"Identikit monsters are boring monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:55:39-07:00","id":1131012,"title":"","content":"My impression of Solar exaltation based on the 3rd Ed core is more that it's something that happens to you, like it did to the heroes of old, and less a chunk of someone from 1500 years ago with all their memories zeroing in on you like one of those flying bombs that Wile E. Coyote turned loose and rewriting your mind/spirit. My read of the book hasn't been exhaustive, but I don't recall seeing anything talking about past life memories with regard to the exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:38:42-07:00","id":1131029,"title":"","content":"Past life memories aren't emphasized (there's no Merit for them, for example), but a couple of places mention it (the description of the Performance ability, also the Craft Charm Art of Permanence and Resistance Charm Willpower-Enhancing Spirit). I think it also shows up in the fluff for Tomb of Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:41:21-07:00","id":1131033,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> <br /> <br /> It is discussed in Miracles of the Solar Exalted. But it is depicted in a more heroic and mystical way than a soul wracking possession. Not that it wouldn't be possible for it to happen like that, but nothing suggests that is the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T00:57:05-07:00","id":1131156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1131012#post1131012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression of Solar exaltation based on the 3rd Ed core is more that it's something that happens to you, like it did to the heroes of old, and less a chunk of someone from 1500 years ago with all their memories zeroing in on you like one of those flying bombs that Wile E. Coyote turned loose and rewriting your mind/spirit. My read of the book hasn't been exhaustive, but I don't recall seeing anything talking about past life memories with regard to the exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the core presents <i>exaltation</i> as a process and barely mentions past lives. You can practically ignore the concept.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bMiracles of the Solar Exalted</b> goes back to referring to exaltation as a discrete soul-widget carrying a spiritual legacy from previous exalted to inheritor. (Though at least describes the transfer as directed by the Unconquered Sun's will rather than automated.) Past lives are presented as more nebulous than concrete; manifesting as <i>deja vu</i> moments and strange dreams rather than memories, or in spirits and sorcerous workings recognising the pattern of solar essence . Then, for all the discussion, Miracles refers to past lives in exactly one charm - the apocryphal <i>Hallowed Bond of Night and Flame</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:05:59-07:00","id":1131491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1130905#post1130905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Solar Essences is that they come with memories from the previous incarnation. It is a common trait in Celestial Essences, but it is particularly important for the Solar Exalted because they may remember the fell pleasures from torturing and violating their Lunar spouses (the theme of extreme physical and psychological abuse is a common one when discussing the relationships, look at the relationship of Lilith and Desus in the First Age). While there are the few Solar Exalted who are blessed without the memories of their previous incarnations, who were the few Solar Exalted who experienced hundreds of incarnations because their Essences were not trapped within the Jade Prison, or who were the few Solar Exalted who actually loved their Lunar consorts, the majority of Solar Exalted should be haunted by the horrible things that they did to their Lunar consorts in their previous incarnation (as well as the horrible things that they did to everyone else as they devolved into corrupted God-Kings).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be extremely careful with that idea. Lytek normally prunes old memories before sending the Exaltations back out to find new hosts. The Solars who do have prior memories are likely ones who were sealed in the Jade Prison without Lytek being able to remove the old memories. Lytek's job has always been memory pruning from the exaltations and it is something he takes great pride in doing. I wouldn't assume every Solar exaltation comes with past life memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6162-raven79","name":"Raven79","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6162_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T19:20:34-07:00","id":1131568,"title":"","content":"If there were 900 Lunars, they would be the single most potent force in Creation and if even half unified they could roflstomp the rest of the Exalted Host combined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T20:49:06-07:00","id":1131592,"title":"","content":"At the very least it would make the narrative of the Solar return overwhelming the Realm's Wyld Hunt make even less sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:56:40-07:00","id":1131760,"title":"","content":"That's a very good point, it'd be a much smaller percentage change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T12:38:18-07:00","id":1131839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1130905#post1130905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Solar Essences is that they come with memories from the previous incarnation. It is a common trait in Celestial Essences, but it is particularly important for the Solar Exalted because they may remember the fell pleasures from torturing and violating their Lunar spouses (the theme of extreme physical and psychological abuse is a common one when discussing the relationships, look at the relationship of Lilith and Desus in the First Age). While there are the few Solar Exalted who are blessed without the memories of their previous incarnations, who were the few Solar Exalted who experienced hundreds of incarnations because their Essences were not trapped within the Jade Prison, or who were the few Solar Exalted who actually loved their Lunar consorts, the majority of Solar Exalted should be haunted by the horrible things that they did to their Lunar consorts in their previous incarnation (as well as the horrible things that they did to everyone else as they devolved into corrupted God-Kings).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As others have noted, this is an extremist view of how bad the Solars got, and to say that almost all Solars tormented and abused, and manipulated their Lunar compinions is...not supported at all in the setting, material, let alone even suggested. Not every Solar is a Desus, and no, extreme physical and psychological abuse is not a common theme in the majority of the relationships. Desus was noted for being a very messed up singularity, and was actively keeping his fellows from finding out what he did to Lilith, that's why she was bound to so many charms. Could some individual Solars be that messed up? Yeah. Look at Arianna's first age incarnation. And yeah, Panther's was absorbed by his own power that he spoke in the name of Sol Invictus with empty authority. But not every Solar was an abusive sociopath. Most Solars were just becoming apathetic to the world because they were seeing themselves as above all things. Negligent...yes. Severly losing touch with the world, for sure. But widespread abusive to the level of what Desus did? Hardly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently homebrewing &quot;<b>Dragon-Blooded 2.75</b>&quot; system.<br /> <br /> Games currently running: <b><a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=47166\" target=\"_blank\">The Throne of Ice</a> - RPoL</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13131-heroofhylia","name":"Heroofhylia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13131_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T11:52:04-08:00","id":1164349,"title":"","content":"Except for the Sidereals, I see no reason in 3E to have a specific number of Exalted. (And for the Sids, that number is a truth I love to violate...)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","na