han 3 months since anybody else was talking about it. Unless you've got a really good reason to revive a thread I think most of us would appreciate leaving stuff alone that's more than a month old. <br /> <br /> It's not a years-dead discussion, but still dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T16:19:11-08:00","id":1164419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164382#post1164382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was only back two pages. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry I am not offended by threadomancy. It didn't used to be so taboo, but somehow its a touchy thing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T17:35:44-08:00","id":1164436,"title":"","content":"Especially considering the thread in question was a troll thread from a poster who got banned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T01:55:06-08:00","id":1164484,"title":"","content":"Why do you say its a troll thread? Yes the poster was banned, but a question is a question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T02:53:57-08:00","id":1164492,"title":"","content":"I don't mind it, someone wants to make an input they can.<br /> <br /> Personally I think it sounds like a very unnecessary change but if it works for the OPs game then go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:11:58-08:00","id":1164498,"title":"","content":"That was my feeling. I don't think it makes the game more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T06:56:43-08:00","id":1164518,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sold on the idea of there being 400 Lunar Exalted. I definitely oppose the idea of 900.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T07:39:42-08:00","id":1164528,"title":"","content":"I was rather fond of the idea of their being one Lunar for each Solar so about 300. But I can get used to 400, it sacrifices a smidge of auspiciousness and harmony in exchange for a smidge more flexibility in the setting.<br /> <br /> 900 is a lot though, the setting would be completely different. But it is still worth discussing, you can even talk about maybe what if most of the Lunar Exaltations spread beyond Creation? So they are in the various worlds created and disconnected after the 1st age. And also populating the deep seas and undergrounds of Creation. And what about a mirror of Creation on the other side of the coin that only has Lunars and Terrestrials? There are a lot to discuss about it, its just going to be a departure, and if the Lunar host ever fully consolidates in Creation Proper they would be the biggest powerblock. Thus even the Solar's ruled they would need the tacit approval of the Silver Host. But with how Solars are only smidge more omnipotent then Lunars it really makes it seem that if their were three times more Lunars then Luna either crippled herself way more then Ignis Divine in creating her Chosen, or she was way mightier (maybe multiple Moons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T08:40:47-08:00","id":1164541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164518#post1164518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sold on the idea of there being 400 Lunar Exalted. I definitely oppose the idea of 900.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main feeling was &quot;oh, that's 1 for every Solar, plus 100 for people who really don't want to be connected to a Solar.&quot; But there's possibly other ways to avoid that issue anyway.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, 400 isn't a big increase, so doesn't make a huge difference either way. 900 though, yeah, that's a massive difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T08:50:58-08:00","id":1164543,"title":"","content":"900 is definitely for a non standard setting, its as drastic as saying there are only 100 Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:03:54-08:00","id":1164547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164541#post1164541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main feeling was &quot;oh, that's 1 for every Solar, plus 100 for people who really don't want to be connected to a Solar.&quot; But there's possibly other ways to avoid that issue anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy feeling since the core came out is that the Bond isn't necessarily even to the same Solar across lifetimes, and you can get plenty of Lunars who used to have it still going in for the whole focusing heavily on something else highly personal to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt seems to me that there must still have been something between Solars and all Lunars for that line about the loss of the Solars having an extreme effect on the Lunars to still hold up.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, this all reminds me of the very earliest days of my interest in Exalted, where somewhere along the way I got the impression that there were two Lunars to every one Solar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:17:32-08:00","id":1164551,"title":"","content":"I always thought that the number of Solars and Lunars both didn't need to be set precisely.<br /> <br /> They made as many as they thought were needed and that amount is known maybe to them alone, or maybe even the Incarnae don't know exactly. The amount wasn't based on how many humanity deserved (because in my take on Sol, there would have been an Exaltation for everyone because he sees infinite potential in everyone) or on how many they could make (because I don't think the amount of Exalted should be based on such... I want to say such a base concept of how hard they are to make?) but on how many would be needed to win the War while making it a hard-fought battle (and again, I think that Sol would state that they needed heroes, and the stuff of heroes was adversity, it couldn't be <i>too easy).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:30:42-08:00","id":1164577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164518#post1164518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sold on the idea of there being 400 Lunar Exalted. I definitely oppose the idea of 900.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just twenty more would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T12:31:59-08:00","id":1164600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164551#post1164551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that the number of Solars and Lunars both didn't need to be set precisely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the canon answer in 3rd edition is about 300 Solars and about 400 Lunars. So it's not precise anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They made as many as they thought were needed and that amount is known maybe to them alone, or maybe even the Incarnae don't know exactly. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... tbh, in the High First Age, it doesn't seem really that hard for the Deliberative to count. Sure, they might miss a few secretive ones, but they'll have got a number somewhere close to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T13:16:30-08:00","id":1164610,"title":"","content":"One of the concerns I have is Luna and the principle of diminishment.<br /> <br /> A Lunar Exaltation may not be exactly as powerful as a Solar Exaltation, but Luna has never been exactly as powerful as Sol. To make more Exalted than him, it seems that she would have diminished herself far beyond his own sacrifice, proportionately.<br /> <br /> Unless he also diminished himself to create the Flame of Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:01:07-08:00","id":1164631,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Law of Diminishment has to be something that affects every single deity on some perfectly proportional system.<br /> It's fine to say &quot;Luna was a bit less powerful than the UCS, he made 300 Solars, he/she/they made 400 Lunars, and today she's a bit less powerful than where he's ended up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe the difference before was smaller than it is now. Maybe making Solars took out far more from him than Lunars did her.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it's a big problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T07:12:15-08:00","id":1164781,"title":"","content":"The principle of diminishment is dumb and does nothing good for anything and can safely be ignored. Which is not to say divinities being diminished is inherently a bad thing, just making arbitrary rules about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T07:22:49-08:00","id":1164784,"title":"","content":"It works for Exigents. I think for the Incarnae, it's the sort of thing that's best just said &quot;yeah, they used to be more powerful than they are now I guess&quot; and left, because doing too much with it wouldn't work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:15:48-08:00","id":1164794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1164781#post1164781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The principle of diminishment is dumb and does nothing good for anything and can safely be ignored. Which is not to say divinities being diminished is inherently a bad thing, just making arbitrary rules about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Its a method to explain why Exalted are the center of attention rather then the Celestines, same with how they made the Yozis consigned to Hell.<br /> <br /> It explains why we don't have infinite Solars ruled over by Infinite Sun God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:39:25-08:00","id":1164796,"title":"","content":"I don't think that really needs an explanation tbh, but I don't mind the idea that Sol could only make 300 Solars, or only would make 300 Solars for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> &quot;Because it made him weaker&quot; just seems a bit dull to me. And the whole thing where there has to be a solid principle of it... like it doesn't need a rule. You could just say &quot;the process of creating an Exigent requires a sacrifice from the God, some are weakened by this, some emboldened by it, some neither, and others are affected in yet more strange ways.&quot; Like I said, the idea of a God diminishing in some way to create something is fine, just as an arbitrary &quot;this always must happen&quot; rule I don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:44:47-08:00","id":1164799,"title":"","content":"They don't give us real crunch for it, it is already just an ambiguous facet of reality. I have no problem for it. It makes sense to me if you want to make an omnipotent shard of empowerment much less a few hundred it feels very fine it takes a toll. How is this different then just saying he could only Create 300 because reasons. Seems more satisfying to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T08:53:05-08:00","id":1164801,"title":"","content":"The way I see the Law of Diminishment working for the Incarna is that the law only mentions that the users are weakened 'somewhat'. That doesn't mean that they lost mystical power, perhaps they lost their potential to make more exalted? This much, and no more. <br /> <br /> Anyway, going to the main thread: in the same way that lunars could not rule the world with being in a 3:1 proportion to sidereals in all this time, I don't see any inherent problem in lunars not automatically ruling the world 3:1 to solars in the Deliberative Age. Following Creation's history, there seem to be many things that work in the 'rule creation' equation other than personal exalted might, with influence over dragon-blooded, yu-shan (temporal power) and the loom (physical infrastructure) being some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T04:48:01-08:00","id":1165013,"title":"","content":"Apologies if I've offended with thread necromancy. My home table is considering our next game-to-be, and since my choice is leaning toward Ex3, I was scrolling through recent-ish threads looking for ideas and news. I thought this one was interesting, so I commented! <br /> <br /> Since the topic has picked back up (thanks!) - and since I'm coming to Ex3 with a clean slate - I think I'd like to see the non-Sidereal Celestials as arising when Destiny and need cross through the same mortal. Maybe (rarely) a new Exaltation. More often a veteran Exaltation sympathetic to that mortal. The total number might be an uncountable mystery, with more and older Exaltations drawn back to Creation during a time of great trouble. Where have they been? Was the Jade Prison actually a prison holding Exaltations inside, or was it a repellent, pushing them away? Couple of ideas to chew on!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T09:20:11-08:00","id":1165067,"title":"","content":"Law of Diminishment is a non-sequitor in this discussion anyhow. Luna making 400-some-odd Lunar Exaltations is probably less to do with whether she could make more or less or make them more powerful and more that 400-some-odd was waht she amde, probably what she could make and probably how she made them resulted in there being 400-some-odd.<br /> <br /> Law of Diminishment is kind of just an extra bit not needed in this particular case, as the Incarna are indivdiually powerful enough that any diminishment is still irrelevant to how powerful they are as beings, and it mostly serves as a plot point on why everyone who can make powerful beings doesn't, and also to add flavor to Exigence more than it really matter sfor other Exalts. Mostly since the Incarna and Dragons are non-actors at this point in teh setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T16:15:27-08:00","id":1165162,"title":"","content":"At my own table there are 425 Lunars and 425 Solars/Abyssals/Infernals - one for each day and night of the year.<br /> <br /> (I considered not counting the 5 days of Calibration, but I don't want to deal with the thousands of &quot;blaze it!&quot; jokes from players)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T18:05:50-08:00","id":1165181,"title":"","content":"I completely forgot about the Calibration caste Sidereals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T21:01:25-08:00","id":1165228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1165162#post1165162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At my own table there are 425 Lunars and 425 Solars/Abyssals/Infernals - one for each day and night of the year.<br /> <br /> (I considered not counting the 5 days of Calibration, but I don't want to deal with the thousands of &amp;quot;blaze it!&amp;quot; jokes from players)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar thought, but I only had 365 of each <br /> <br /> Things were different before the War","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T18:46:34-08:00","id":1174428,"title":"","content":"<b>EDIT:</b> Nevermind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-08-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T19:15:14-08:00","id":1174435,"title":"","content":"The honest issue I have with tripling the number of Lunars is - why? In a shared universe (i.e. a hypothetical - and very insane - Exalted LARP that was played on the scope of OWbN or MES), an increase in the number of Exaltations may make sense. In Exalted as it is, though, even if you Monster-of-the-Weeked Lunars, you'd have more than enough for a game of any decent length (hell, even in a weekly game that kills off five a week for some reason, you still get a whole year of play with just 300 Lunars, without reincarnation).<br /> <br /> Maybe there is a good reason to expand the numbers, but there needs to be that reason. There were fewer Sidereals because they were meant to teach multiple Celestials each, and because their manipulations of Fate were arguably too dangerous to allow more than that. The number of Lunars and Solars seem small, but are supposed to to make each one feel unique. So, the real question is - what do you really achieve by increasing the number to 900? If there is something specific, great. If not, if you can achieve your plot aims within the 300 you do have, I'd go in a different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T05:40:01-08:00","id":1174832,"title":"","content":"We can sit with &quot;there's a few hundred&quot; and not delve further into it. Mythic threads need no spreadsheets.<br /> <br /> The one specificity I'd add, if it's not already canon, is that there are exactly as many solars as there are lunars. They're interwoven like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:11:31-08:00","id":1174842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1129502-increasing-the-number-of-lunar-exalted?p=1174832#post1174832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can sit with &quot;there's a few hundred&quot; and not delve further into it. Mythic threads need no spreadsheets.<br /> <br /> The one specificity I'd add, if it's not already canon, is that there are exactly as many solars as there are lunars. They're interwoven like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The previous devs had the Solars/Abyssals/Infernals total at around 300, and the Lunars at around 400, drawing on 1e's Storyteller's Companion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:31:43-08:00","id":1174850,"title":"","content":"Then it's my homebrew instead of canon. Life is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:35:59-08:00","id":1174851,"title":"","content":"There's exactly 350 of each. Solars are hard to keep track of and lunar shapeshifting means some of them got counted twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:54:46-08:00","id":1175386,"title":"","content":"Your story can be however you like it. If you want more, make more! Its mostly fluff. A question may come up regarding &quot;how was Lunar capable of making more Exaltations than the Sun? Was the Moon more powerful, or did they find a way to break the law and rules (which would be a very lunar thing to do).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I always went on my assumption that there were:<br /> 300 Solar Souls which have been diluted into:<br /> &lt;151 Solars<br /> &gt; 99 Abyssals<br /> &gt; 50 Infernals<br /> <i>*: This ivariable totals is due to the set 300 Solar Souls being converted/ Corrupted into Abyssals and Infernal - meaning I suspect there are LESS than 150 Solar Souls active... though maybe with powerful charms the Abyssals and Infernals could be 'changed back' somehow??</i><br /> <br /> Of these 300, there are 60 of each CASTE TYPE (so the total number of Dawn, Dusk and Slayer Souls combined would add up to 60).<br /> <br /> <br /> 300 Lunars - due to their &quot;moonsilver tattoos&quot; they could ALL be one Caste, though I like to assume each has around 90-110 per caste - with approximately 10 Lunars of each Caste supervising the wyld of each of the 9 corners of creation, while the remainder roam the center of Creation and do thei thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 300/ 300 for me implied the Sun and Moon were equals in many ways. Which I personally like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 100 Sidereals, divided into 20 per Caste. While small in number, each was made by a single God lesser in power than the Sun or Moon. Their role was likely to run interference during the war so the &quot;Creators&quot; wouldn't see it coming until the Exalted were ready to strike.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Dragon Bloods have as many as they can produce. The power is in the blood - not the Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T03:45:15-08:00","id":1175410,"title":"","content":"Solars are a bit stronger than Lunars, so if you want Sol and Luna to be equal it actually makes sense for there to be more lunars. 300 X = 400 Y.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could also have it that in terms of raw power Luna has Conky beat, but that Conky makes up for it thanks to his theme being Perfection. He does more with less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T04:10:31-08:00","id":1175414,"title":"","content":"That goes against the whole gravitas that the sun has in mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T04:21:02-08:00","id":1175417,"title":"","content":"Is there really a need to dig like this into explanations?<br /> I mean, the canon is clear: there's a few hundreds of each.<br /> <br /> You want more lunars, but not too many? Just add them. Like, really. There's nothing to be felt there. The setting doesn't crumble. It won't be perceived by players. Just put them there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}